{"schemaVersion":1,"generatedAt":"2026-08-16T16:20:46.501Z","id":"627cd50f826c14d6b5e44ed9","canonicalUrl":"https://lore.kernel.org/r/20260727073431.2019724-1-daniel.turull%40ericsson.com/","channels":["openembedded-core"],"thread":{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"thread:lore-git:20260727073431.2019724-1-daniel.turull@ericsson.com","source":{"kind":"static-generated","canonicalThreadUrl":"https://lore.kernel.org/r/20260727073431.2019724-1-daniel.turull%40ericsson.com/","fetchedAt":"2026-08-16T16:20:46.501Z","contentDigest":"lore-git:20260727073431.2019724-1-daniel.turull@ericsson.com"},"subject":"Re: [wrynose][PATCH] libarchive: fix CVE-2026-14164","messages":{"0447ebc9d29b0736de8ba0c75f155ed4f880d072.camel@pbarker.dev":{"id":"0447ebc9d29b0736de8ba0c75f155ed4f880d072.camel@pbarker.dev","messageId":"0447ebc9d29b0736de8ba0c75f155ed4f880d072.camel@pbarker.dev","references":["20260727073431.2019724-1-daniel.turull@ericsson.com"],"missingAncestorIds":["20260727073431.2019724-1-daniel.turull@ericsson.com"],"author":{"name":"Paul Barker","address":"paul@pbarker.dev"},"replyTo":[],"to":[{"name":"","address":"daniel.turull@ericsson.com"},{"name":"","address":"openembedded-core@lists.openembedded.org"}],"cc":[],"timestamp":{"raw":"2026-08-16T09:32:52.000Z","iso":"2026-08-16T09:32:52.000Z","valid":true},"subject":"Re: [wrynose][PATCH] libarchive: fix CVE-2026-14164","mailingLists":[{"id":"openembedded-core.lists.openembedded.org","displayName":"openembedded-core.lists.openembedded.org"}],"blocks":[{"kind":"quote","attribution":"On Mon, 2026-07-27 at 09:34 +0200, daniel.turull@ericsson.com wrote:","lines":[{"depth":1,"text":"From: Daniel Turull <daniel.turull@ericsson.com>"},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"Backport patch to fix CVE-2026-14164."},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"References:"},{"depth":1,"text":"  https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-14164"},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"Upstream fix:"},{"depth":1,"text":"  https://github.com/libarchive/libarchive/commit/f774f03b40cb109348e5c6d52b59c864e3cfa8e8"},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"Tested with ptest:"},{"depth":1,"text":"Before: PASSED: 5, FAILED: 0, SKIPPED: 0"},{"depth":1,"text":"After: PASSED: 5, FAILED: 0, SKIPPED: 0"},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"Signed-off-by: Daniel Turull <daniel.turull@ericsson.com>"},{"depth":1,"text":"---"},{"depth":1,"text":" .../libarchive/CVE-2026-14164.patch           | 53 +++++++++++++++++++"},{"depth":1,"text":" .../libarchive/libarchive_3.8.7.bb            |  1 +"},{"depth":1,"text":" 2 files changed, 54 insertions(+)"},{"depth":1,"text":" create mode 100644 meta/recipes-extended/libarchive/libarchive/CVE-2026-14164.patch"},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"diff --git a/meta/recipes-extended/libarchive/libarchive/CVE-2026-14164.patch b/meta/recipes-extended/libarchive/libarchive/CVE-2026-14164.patch"},{"depth":1,"text":"new file mode 100644"},{"depth":1,"text":"index 0000000000..b734fc448f"},{"depth":1,"text":"--- /dev/null"},{"depth":1,"text":"+++ b/meta/recipes-extended/libarchive/libarchive/CVE-2026-14164.patch"},{"depth":1,"text":"@@ -0,0 +1,53 @@"},{"depth":1,"text":"+From edbac77e8e544286fe7581bc398781c949ee5a22 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001"},{"depth":1,"text":"+From: \"Dustin L. Howett\" <dustin@howett.net>"},{"depth":1,"text":"+Date: Sun, 24 May 2026 12:43:00 -0500"},{"depth":1,"text":"+Subject: [PATCH] Merge pull request #3071 from stoeckmann/rar5_doublefree"},{"depth":1,"text":"+"},{"depth":1,"text":"+rar5: Avoid dangling pointers in init_unpack"},{"depth":1,"text":"+(cherry picked from commit 42453cf16255800726b4efedab25138639ceef20)"},{"depth":1,"text":"+"},{"depth":1,"text":"+Conflicts Resolved:"},{"depth":1,"text":"+"},{"depth":1,"text":"+libarchive/archive_read_support_format_rar5.c (1 conflict):"},{"depth":1,"text":"+- The stable branch's init_unpack() already unconditionally NULLs"},{"depth":1,"text":"+  rar->cstate.window_buf and rar->cstate.filtered_buf right after free()"},{"depth":1,"text":"+  (the core CVE fix), but still retained the redundant else-branch that"},{"depth":1,"text":"+  re-NULLed them when window_size <= 0. Removed that dead else-branch to"},{"depth":1,"text":"+  match the upstream fix, and omitted upstream's added"},{"depth":1,"text":"+  `if(...== NULL) return ARCHIVE_FATAL;` calloc failure checks, since"},{"depth":1,"text":"+  init_unpack() is void-returning in this stable version and predates"},{"depth":1,"text":"+  that hardening."},{"depth":1,"text":"+"},{"depth":1,"text":"+Assisted-by: kiro:claude-sonnet-5"},{"depth":1,"text":"+"},{"depth":1,"text":"+Changes from upstream commit f774f03b40cb:"},{"depth":1,"text":"+  - libarchive/archive_read_support_format_rar5.c: adapted from upstream"},{"depth":1,"text":"+"},{"depth":1,"text":"+CVE: CVE-2026-14164"},{"depth":1,"text":"+Upstream-Status: Backport [https://github.com/libarchive/libarchive/commit/f774f03b40cb109348e5c6d52b59c864e3cfa8e8]"},{"depth":1,"text":"+"},{"depth":1,"text":"+Signed-off-by: Daniel Turull <daniel.turull@ericsson.com>"},{"depth":1,"text":"+---"},{"depth":1,"text":"+ libarchive/archive_read_support_format_rar5.c | 6 +++---"},{"depth":1,"text":"+ 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)"},{"depth":1,"text":"+"},{"depth":1,"text":"+diff --git a/libarchive/archive_read_support_format_rar5.c b/libarchive/archive_read_support_format_rar5.c"},{"depth":1,"text":"+index 63dd97b3..271aa0cb 100644"},{"depth":1,"text":"+--- a/libarchive/archive_read_support_format_rar5.c"},{"depth":1,"text":"++++ b/libarchive/archive_read_support_format_rar5.c"},{"depth":1,"text":"+@@ -2568,12 +2568,12 @@ static void init_unpack(struct rar5* rar) {"},{"depth":1,"text":"+ \tfree(rar->cstate.window_buf);"},{"depth":1,"text":"+ \tfree(rar->cstate.filtered_buf);"},{"depth":1,"text":"+ "},{"depth":1,"text":"++\trar->cstate.window_buf = NULL;"},{"depth":1,"text":"++\trar->cstate.filtered_buf = NULL;"},{"depth":1,"text":"++"},{"depth":1,"text":"+ \tif(rar->cstate.window_size > 0) {"},{"depth":1,"text":"+ \t\trar->cstate.window_buf = calloc(1, rar->cstate.window_size);"},{"depth":1,"text":"+ \t\trar->cstate.filtered_buf = calloc(1, rar->cstate.window_size);"},{"depth":1,"text":"+-\t} else {"},{"depth":1,"text":"+-\t\trar->cstate.window_buf = NULL;"},{"depth":1,"text":"+-\t\trar->cstate.filtered_buf = NULL;"},{"depth":1,"text":"+ \t}"},{"depth":1,"text":"+ "},{"depth":1,"text":"+ \tclear_data_ready_stack(rar);"}],"lineCount":80,"maximumDepth":1},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Hi Daniel,"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"The above fix didn't make sense to me, so I looked in to the CVE. The\ninitial report [1] says:"},{"kind":"code","text":"    The issue occurs when parsing a valid RAR5 archive that exercises\n    the filter path. During decompression, rar->cstate.filtered_buf can\n    be assigned to a filter output buffer. Later, when libarchive\n    processes a subsequent file and reinitializes the unpacking state,\n    init_unpack() frees the existing filtered_buf but does not clear the\n    pointer."},{"kind":"code","text":"    If the following allocation fails, init_unpack() returns\n    ARCHIVE_FATAL while rar->cstate.filtered_buf still contains a\n    dangling pointer. When the caller later releases the archive object,\n    rar5_cleanup() frees the same pointer again, resulting in a\n    double-free."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"[1]: https://github.com/libarchive/libarchive/issues/3069"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"The `return ARCHIVE_FATAL` paths are not present in libarchive 3.8.7, so\nthe function can't return between while rar->cstate.filtered_buf is\nstill a dangling pointer."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Let me know if you agree with that analysis, if so then perhaps we can\nhandle this via CVE_STATUS."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Best regards,"},{"kind":"signature","text":"Paul Barker","lineCount":1}],"patchIds":[],"attachmentMetadata":[],"sourceOrdinal":0,"diagnostics":[],"declaredParentMessageId":"20260727073431.2019724-1-daniel.turull@ericsson.com"}},"rootIds":["0447ebc9d29b0736de8ba0c75f155ed4f880d072.camel@pbarker.dev"],"childrenByParent":{},"chronologicalIds":["0447ebc9d29b0736de8ba0c75f155ed4f880d072.camel@pbarker.dev"],"patchSeries":[],"diagnostics":[],"patches":{}}}